The '''2026–27 Duke Blue Devils men's basketball team''' will represent [[Duke University]] during the [[2026–27 NCAA Division I men's basketball season]]. The [[Duke Blue Devils|Blue Devils]] will be led by fifth-year head coach [[Jon Scheyer]]. Duke plays their home games at [[Cameron Indoor Stadium]] in [[Durham, North Carolina]], as a member of the [[Atlantic Coast Conference]] (ACC).

== Previous season ==
{{Main|2025–26 Duke Blue Devils men's basketball team}}
The Blue Devils finished the 2025–26 season {{Win-loss record|w=35|l=3}} and {{Win-loss record|w=17|l=1}} in ACC play to finish in first place. As the first seed in the [[2026 ACC men's basketball tournament|ACC Tournament]], held at the [[Spectrum Center]] in [[Charlotte, North Carolina]], they earned a bye to the quarterfinals and narrowly beat [[2025–26 Florida State Seminoles men's basketball team|Florida State]], 80–79, to advance to the semifinals.<ref>{{cite web |title=Top-Seeded Duke Wins Thriller, 80-79, over Florida State in ACC Quarterfinal |url=https://goduke.com/news/2026/3/12/mens-basketball-top-seeded-duke-wins-thriller-80-79-over-florida-state-in-acc-quarterfinal |website=goduke.com |publisher=[[Duke University]] Athletics |date=12 March 2026}}</ref> There, they defeated [[2025–26 Clemson Tigers men's basketball team|Clemson]] 73–61 to advance to the championship game,<ref>{{cite web |title=No. 1 Duke Defeats Clemson, 73-61, to Advance to ACC Title Game |url=https://goduke.com/news/2026/3/14/mens-basketball-no-1-duke-defeats-clemson-73-61-to-advance-to-acc-title-game |website=goduke.com |publisher=[[Duke University]] Athletics |date=14 March 2026}}</ref> where they defeated [[2025–26 Virginia Cavaliers men's basketball team|Virginia]], 74–70, to win the tournament championship.<ref>{{cite web |title=Duke Repeats as Men’s Basketball ACC Champions |url=https://goduke.com/news/2026/3/14/mens-basketball-duke-repeats-as-mens-basketball-acc-champions |website=goduke.com |publisher=[[Duke University]] Athletics |date=14 March 2026}}</ref> The championship was their 24th conference tournament victory in program history and their second consecutive championship. As a result, they received the conference's automatic bid to the [[NCAA Division I men's basketball tournament upsets|NCAA tournament]] as the [[2026 NCAA Division I men's basketball tournament|No. 1 overall seed]], and were placed in the East region. In the first round, the Blue Devils trailed No. 16 seed [[2025–26 Siena Saints men's basketball team|Siena]] 43–32 at halftime, becoming the first No. 1 seed to trail a 16 seed by double-digits at the half in tournament history.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/story/_/id/48278903/sources-syracuse-hire-gerry-mcnamara-basketball-coach|title=Sources: Syracuse to hire Gerry McNamara as basketball coach|accessdate=March 22, 2026|date=March 22, 2026|publisher=[[ESPN]]|last1=Thamel|first1=Pete|author-link1=Pete Thamel|last2=Brozello|first2=Jeff}}</ref> However, they rallied to escape the upset to win 71–65.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hale |first=David |date=2026-03-19 |title=Duke avoids historic upset, stops Siena in NCAA tournament |url=https://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/story/_/id/48252405/duke-avoids-historic-upset-stops-siena-ncaa-tournament |access-date=2026-03-20 |website=ESPN.com |language=en}}</ref> The Blue Devils proceeded to defeat No. 9 seed [[2025–26 TCU Horned Frogs men's basketball team|TCU]] 81–58 in the second round<ref>{{cite web |title=Duke Marches into Sweet 16 by Topping TCU |url=https://goduke.com/news/2026/3/21/mens-basketball-duke-marches-into-sweet-16-by-topping-tcu |website=goduke.com |publisher=[[Duke University]] Athletics |date=21 March 2026}}</ref> and No. 5 seed [[2025–26 St. John's Red Storm men's basketball team|St. John's]] 80–75 in the Sweet Sixteen.<ref>{{cite web |title=Duke Bound for Elite Eight After Topping St. John’s, 80-75 |url=https://goduke.com/news/2026/3/27/mens-basketball-duke-bound-for-elite-eight-after-topping-st-johns-80-75 |website=goduke.com |publisher=[[Duke University]] Athletics |date=27 March 2026}}</ref> Against No. 2 seed [[2025–26 UConn Huskies men's basketball team|UConn]] in the Elite Eight, the Blue Devils took a 19-point lead. However, the Huskies pulled off a comeback in the final seconds, where UConn's [[Silas Demary Jr.]] deflected a pass from [[Cayden Boozer]], leading to Huskies guard [[Braylon Mullins]] making a game-winning [[Glossary of basketball terms#logo three|logo]] [[Three-point field goal|three]] with 0.4 seconds left, to win 73–72.<ref>{{Cite news |last= |first= |date=March 29, 2026 |title=Inside UConn's stunning win over Duke in Sunday's Elite Eight|url=https://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/story/_/id/48335596/march-madness-predictions-live-tracker-elite-eight-michigan-duke-uconn-2026 |access-date=March 29, 2026 |website=espn.com|publisher=[[ESPN]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Shaughnessy |first=Dan |date=April 3, 2026 |title=You'll always remember where you were when Braylon Mullins shot UConn into Final Four, and other thoughts|url=https://www.bostonglobe.com/2026/04/03/sports/braylon-mullins-uconn-basketball/ |access-date=April 4, 2026 |website=bostonglobe.com|publisher=[[The Boston Globe]]}}</ref>

== Offseason ==
On March 19, 2026, assistant coach [[Evan Bradds]] was hired as the head coach of the [[Belmont Bruins men's basketball|Belmont Bruins]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Belmont Names Evan Bradds Head Men's Basketball Coach |url=https://belmontbruins.com/news/2026/3/19/belmont-names-evan-bradds-head-mens-basketball-coach.aspx |website=belmontbruins.com |publisher=[[Belmont University]] Athletics |date=19 March 2026}}</ref> He remained with Duke throughout the [[2026 NCAA Division I men's basketball tournament|2026 NCAA tournament]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Borzello|first=Jeff|date=2026-03-19 |title=Sources: Belmont finalizing hire of Duke's Evan Bradds as coach |url=https://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/story/_/id/48244492/sources-belmont-finalizing-hire-duke-evan-bradds-coach |access-date=2026-03-19 |website=espn.com|publisher=[[ESPN]] |language=en}}</ref>

